fe05da7-7615-525d-874d-5edaadde1a14" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461078}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73083626-cc38-5982-9c18-9459efa65b4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95572" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{y}^{2}=2y+{y}^{3}.$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(x)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}+{y}^{2}+2y,\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)={y}^{3}+{y}^{2}+2y.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=0$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(0)={0}^{3}+{0}^{2}+2(0)=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=1$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)={1}^{3}+{1}^{2}+2(1)=4\\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=2$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(2)={2}^{3}+{2}^{2}+2(2)=16\\ne 0.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=0$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "800be69e-608d-5075-b31f-11000aa9ed10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165897} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd4fd9b-7aa6-5c68-913c-723aa1196de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165898} {:answer/id #uuid "a563265f-c736-5040-a362-b9d3ab741069" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165899} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9f6d6f-3ddb-5e3f-b56f-0c9a591bc0c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165900} {:answer/id #uuid "6c023715-983f-5be4-8c60-cfa03b085c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165901}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b9e9f3bd-3d0b-558a-8525-b0ee37aff66f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165896}] :question/id #uuid "0faf8e9d-c46b-5d05-a98c-526f6252b54e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96071" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dt} - \\cos y = 0$. Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n\n1. $y = π$\n2. $y = \\frac{π}{2}$\n3. $y = 0$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10fbd1fd-81d6-5ab9-9a42-0df9f96eda22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465285} {:answer/id #uuid "1395580a-0ad4-5646-9291-c0acb3fea193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10fbd1fd-81d6-5ab9-9a42-0df9f96eda22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465285} :answer-field/id #uuid "84ac4b21-d3c8-5ac0-b070-d7d504bcc850" :answer-field/key "$y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccfd9b16-57d1-5331-8023-5fa2705b3253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465287} {:answer/id #uuid "047f3772-89f4-5fce-a998-333acb699eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccfd9b16-57d1-5331-8023-5fa2705b3253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465287} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b2cdc27-e594-5f5c-81a3-b5b4ae2af15d" :answer-field/key "$y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1f86228-76ce-5ad6-8dba-2e38cc396dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465289} {:answer/id #uuid "f3293a37-b3c5-57c9-8cd2-7bebc9961197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3293a37-b3c5-57c9-8cd2-7bebc9961197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465290} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6eadc1-e12f-5563-a5fe-c1f034620e4e" :answer-field/key "$y=\\pi $" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466488}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c7b0ec58-a026-543f-8622-101c6f9cdc96" :question/math-academy-id "q-160419" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\pi .$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(t)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y+\\pi ,\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y+\\pi .$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=0$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-0+\\pi =\\pi \\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $$\n\\displaystyle f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi =1+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\ne 0.\n$$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=\\pi $ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(\\pi )=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\pi +\\pi =0-\\pi +\\pi =0.$$\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=\\pi $ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278295 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53189a57-4a52-569c-b4e6-971a16c99c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465291} {:answer/id #uuid "2ffce523-690d-5d3f-ade2-3f244c6d6161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ffce523-690d-5d3f-ade2-3f244c6d6161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465292} :answer-field/id #uuid "247493c4-7128-51e9-9e5c-5ea79e484ddb" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c7feaaa-a4a2-57fb-b6b2-dfc3fcb0aa5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465293} {:answer/id #uuid "b59ae2a3-7e6e-513d-95bd-ba5c448d88bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b59ae2a3-7e6e-513d-95bd-ba5c448d88bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465294} :answer-field/id #uuid "51ca2add-20e1-5ed3-9359-fea868180b27" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466490} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceec5708-f222-5686-b123-0c46ad5f48b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465295} {:answer/id #uuid "fb17ae72-76f4-5cdd-9d25-d53e0e9875f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceec5708-f222-5686-b123-0c46ad5f48b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465295} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8f19a1b-9d84-5e40-900d-78c7d390c63f" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466491}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09328241-3b39-5707-a62b-8ca38e3a3a9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-160422" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}=1.\n$$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(x)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)=1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=-1$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(-1)=1-\\frac{1}{(-1)^{2}}=1-1=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=1$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)=1-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}=1-1=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=2$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $$\n\\displaystyle f(2)=1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}=\\frac{3}{4}\\ne 0.\n$$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=-1$; $y=1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8139637-8e82-5b32-b05d-a90a5ed25604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469806} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b99b14-815f-5b95-84f7-bf5e12833ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6b99b14-815f-5b95-84f7-bf5e12833ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469807} :answer-field/id #uuid "792054a2-6470-5383-8af1-815b20b190b7" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470515} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b5002f-0058-5055-8f76-cd09fc58fc68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469808} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5cd59b-8c99-5170-8de8-87b5f99f1eca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18b5002f-0058-5055-8f76-cd09fc58fc68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469808} :answer-field/id #uuid "86b22de7-7fe7-5dd4-b362-42d2cacff149" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470516} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c45e6e66-7fbc-5337-9c2b-a5fa36cf9618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469810} {:answer/id #uuid "308fcee5-5e70-5885-b5ea-20cdebf40a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c45e6e66-7fbc-5337-9c2b-a5fa36cf9618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469810} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3426a6c-4972-5b04-aaed-80a5d1606fef" :answer-field/key "$y=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470517}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4bdcd03c-4e33-5af2-a43a-72ec614b803e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96070" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+y={y}^{2}-2.$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(t)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}={y}^{2}-y-2,\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)={y}^{2}-y-2.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=2$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(2)={2}^{2}-2-2=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=1$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)={1}^{2}-1-2=-2\\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=4$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(4)={4}^{2}-4-2=10\\ne 0.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e089712-9e8d-5a06-9486-b36e393637d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469812} {:answer/id #uuid "e5af46c0-36b4-5041-b26e-4967d1519a68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e089712-9e8d-5a06-9486-b36e393637d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469812} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0be3825-bbe9-533b-835f-a228584ff886" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "260410a8-65bb-5892-aa51-d356fbb9b5a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469814} {:answer/id #uuid "2431bdce-8758-5311-bac2-20c5ea1f09ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2431bdce-8758-5311-bac2-20c5ea1f09ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469815} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7b1200c-89e7-56eb-8bd9-0a9a36df85a5" :answer-field/key "$y=e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ceb5c2b-15b4-5a91-8b04-6a949d64834d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469816} {:answer/id #uuid "7f9bff13-8c86-5ea9-a24a-7a92868f1e4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ceb5c2b-15b4-5a91-8b04-6a949d64834d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469816} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca4bcc5-b73b-5b70-b7a2-6076a97d7f00" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470520}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7617131b-e756-503f-ac7c-f76ae1870fab" :question/math-academy-id "q-96072" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{2}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$ Which of the following is an equilibrium solution of this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given an autonomous differential equation ${y}^{′}(x)=f(y),$ if there exists a constant $c$ such that $f(c)=0,$ then $y=c$ is an equilibrium solution of the equation.\n\nFirst, we write the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-{e}^{2},\n$$\n\nand we get that $f(y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-{e}^{2}.$\n\nNow, let's check each proposed solution by substituting them into $f(y).$\n\n- $y=1$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(1)=(1)^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡1-{e}^{2}=-{e}^{2}\\ne 0.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- $y=e$ is an equilibrium point. We have $f(e)={e}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-{e}^{2}={e}^{2}-{e}^{2}=0.$$\\,✓$\n\n- $y=2$ is *not* an equilibrium point. We have $f(2)={2}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-{e}^{2}\\ne 0.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=e$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "081fe611-f9c4-5acb-882f-b5e03236b641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693813} {:answer/id #uuid "359fb584-6afb-590c-af73-9a22b571007b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "081fe611-f9c4-5acb-882f-b5e03236b641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693813} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b167e5f-f0c3-5152-a6ba-438cc5ab5335" :answer-field/key "$y=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b9e558-4486-53b2-bf75-e7477059b381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693812} {:answer/id #uuid "9787754d-5a34-556a-a14d-14d3a1c8b41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9787754d-5a34-556a-a14d-14d3a1c8b41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693829} :answer-field/id #uuid "8653240a-921c-5fce-9fa8-dcde31d6cac4" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693828} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd7b7b6-d446-5fa9-900b-a4ae7afbe118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693816} {:answer/id #uuid "5d86a352-9b64-5091-b446-3b9bafcf6ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d86a352-9b64-5091-b446-3b9bafcf6ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693825} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9cb2044-0cef-5134-87a2-b0f4f5557b47" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693839}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14d3798c-89a1-52dc-bb0c-ee927b19593c" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=y^2-y-2.\n$$\n\nA constant function $y(t)=c$ is an equilibrium solution when substituting $y=c$ makes the right-hand side zero.\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a constant function $y(t)=c$, we have $dy/dt=0$. Thus we test whether $f(c)=0$, where $f(y)=y^2-y-2$.\n\n- For $y=-1$, $f(-1)=(-1)^2-(-1)-2=0$, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n- For $y=0$, $f(0)=0^2-0-2=-2\\ne0$, so this is not an equilibrium solution.\n- For $y=2$, $f(2)=2^2-2-2=0$, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-1$ and $y=2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "569c7c75-f7ad-579b-a3b0-88f16169cc5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693823} {:answer/id #uuid "a2af7ae9-101e-57c4-86f1-29713594b503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2af7ae9-101e-57c4-86f1-29713594b503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693831} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfc3ba59-9e59-53bd-a29d-a0f4938abd9e" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f32f91a-7190-5ba7-9dfa-cdee0daf85a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693818} {:answer/id #uuid "de14998d-03f7-52b8-9b35-f541b291b322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de14998d-03f7-52b8-9b35-f541b291b322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693836} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a8ac6a-5e59-5881-88e1-166b9623262d" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2e24c25-7dc0-5b7a-9882-b4fdfda885c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693835} {:answer/id #uuid "e11aaf8e-73b9-5fd5-94a6-e4cad02e74a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2e24c25-7dc0-5b7a-9882-b4fdfda885c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693835} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecdea050-e64c-5a0f-a90e-17d3261cacfd" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693838}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f478031-2352-577f-be54-374bed10f978" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}+y(y-1)=2(y-1).\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative zero. Isolate the derivative to identify the function whose value must be zero:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=2(y-1)-y(y-1)=(y-1)(2-y).\n$$\n\nWrite $f(y)=(y-1)(2-y)$ and test each proposed constant.\n\n- For $y=-1$, $f(-1)=(-2)(3)=-6\\ne0$, so this is not an equilibrium solution.\n- For $y=1$, $f(1)=0(1)=0$, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n- For $y=2$, $f(2)=1(0)=0$, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=1$ and $y=2$. The derivative is zero when the two sides of the original equation balance; its individual terms need not be zero."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76e612f4-79d9-5dab-9577-2b538b75ba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693826} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6b08c7-7689-585b-a37a-6760707ff310" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76e612f4-79d9-5dab-9577-2b538b75ba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693826} :answer-field/id #uuid "035c6f83-1dc6-5ff1-b741-c779fae9d7a8" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c1d7c0f-60bd-54db-928a-237785d83fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693820} {:answer/id #uuid "5786a637-2e37-5611-84d2-26e4a908f133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c1d7c0f-60bd-54db-928a-237785d83fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693820} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b99e832-8aea-5ba1-bd58-d416262a5c24" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08578261-62f0-567e-b368-25d5fd7ca27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693814} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ea0440-59c7-5b60-8cf4-45eb69c165fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4ea0440-59c7-5b60-8cf4-45eb69c165fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693832} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e62b53e-e17d-5990-b8be-a582ffe7fc0f" :answer-field/key "$y=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693827}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9bd066c2-0ef8-5d1a-97bd-beded6087834" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=\\frac{y^2-y-2}{y+1}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An equilibrium solution $y(t)=c$ must be in the domain of the original differential equation and make its right-hand side zero. Here the denominator requires $c\\ne-1$.\n\n- For $y=-1$, the denominator is zero. Although the numerator is also zero, the original right-hand side is undefined. This is not a solution.\n- For $y=2$, the denominator is $3\\ne0$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{2^2-2-2}{2+1}=\\frac{0}{3}=0,\n$$\n\nso this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=1$, the right-hand side is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1^2-1-2}{1+1}=\\frac{-2}{2}=-1\\ne0,\n$$\n\nso this is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nFactoring gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2-y-2}{y+1}=\\frac{(y-2)(y+1)}{y+1}=y-2,\\qquad y\\ne-1.\n$$\n\nCancellation does not restore the excluded value $y=-1$. Select only $y=2$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025a6a8d-f6bf-5bbb-930a-fba18024f79c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694165} {:answer/id #uuid "99cd846f-df17-5633-8327-3e5ce3f10691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "025a6a8d-f6bf-5bbb-930a-fba18024f79c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694165} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c8346bd-4519-5754-af6d-9140b9e4d49d" :answer-field/key "$y=e^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694167} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "013476bc-608e-525d-9508-262561220d1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694164} {:answer/id #uuid "f941ef2a-1c02-5a88-9ce8-27c2900202b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f941ef2a-1c02-5a88-9ce8-27c2900202b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694212} :answer-field/id #uuid "58661899-0be5-50f0-89da-a03cf77e9640" :answer-field/key "$y=e$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694178} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "468e2afa-c88d-50a4-8a63-fc09dedf003b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694175} {:answer/id #uuid "8d27a7d5-9167-5ea4-94a6-4ec3782a1107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "468e2afa-c88d-50a4-8a63-fc09dedf003b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694175} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fb533cd-f187-5a47-82fc-9053c43a2ca5" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694179}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a34103f-c714-5964-8bdd-43da1a58a11e" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = y^{2} \\ln{\\left(y \\right)} + e^{-2}.\n$$\n\nA constant function $y(t)=c$ is an **equilibrium solution** when it is in the domain of the equation and makes the derivative zero.\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nThe original equation requires $y>0$.\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=e$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e \\right)} \\\\  &= 1 \\\\ L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= c^{2} \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} + e^{-2} \\\\  &= e^{-2} + e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=e^{-1}$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(e^{-1} \\right)} \\\\  &= -1 \\\\ L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= c^{2} \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} + e^{-2} \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln{\\left(c \\right)} &= \\ln{\\left(1 \\right)} \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= c^{2} \\ln{\\left(c \\right)} + e^{-2} \\\\  &= e^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=e^{-1}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3953d2d4-618c-5ceb-a969-ce0f5f8b85b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694174} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f903a5-082e-516e-b669-ed0b0162a92a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9f903a5-082e-516e-b669-ed0b0162a92a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694213} :answer-field/id #uuid "166645af-317a-5a10-8bb7-e430ab5a7faa" :answer-field/key "$y=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b50709-90a5-5b99-81c7-715d0ab290e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694177} {:answer/id #uuid "f34903bc-0a94-56e5-864a-609484550a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57b50709-90a5-5b99-81c7-715d0ab290e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694177} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ebd37e-5e2d-5c18-93b3-4987c92c4178" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bda0e8b4-1d08-502b-8ca6-4f2c95522d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694201} {:answer/id #uuid "cc43475d-db7e-54b5-ad74-caa778172515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bda0e8b4-1d08-502b-8ca6-4f2c95522d83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694201} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfa3f277-7dd8-596e-96a0-fdd8e9f74cf6" :answer-field/key "$y=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694204}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2020e3e6-1568-5a63-a4fe-250b51c7ba6d" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = 2 y^{2} - 4 y - 6.\n$$\n\nA constant function $y(t)=c$ is an **equilibrium solution** when it is in the domain of the equation and makes the derivative zero.\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A constant function $y(t)=c$ has derivative $dy/dt=0$. It must satisfy the original equation and its domain restrictions.\n\nTest each supplied constant in the original equation, with the derivative set to zero.\n\n- For $y=c=-1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= 2 c^{2} - 4 c - 6 \\\\  &= 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values agree, so this is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=1$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= 2 c^{2} - 4 c - 6 \\\\  &= -8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $y=c=4$, evaluate the non-derivative left and right sides, denoted $L(c)$ and $R(c)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(c) &= 0 \\\\  &= 0 \\\\ R(c) &= 2 c^{2} - 4 c - 6 \\\\  &= 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe values differ, so this is *not* an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=-1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186694194 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a89beed6-7dee-5d4a-899a-c385ac44957b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694193} {:answer/id #uuid "b9dbf626-2b95-5441-bfbd-b9f9be9ff984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a89beed6-7dee-5d4a-899a-c385ac44957b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694193} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dd3945c-be43-5496-add3-0e5e3400ac3f" :answer-field/key "$y=e^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84ff0bd4-f953-5c49-bf5e-ee533d15c963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694184} {:answer/id #uuid "d77cf4b9-42b0-5569-957b-ff4b4224e2bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d77cf4b9-42b0-5569-957b-ff4b4224e2bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186694205} :answer-field/id #uuid "90d7dc39-2ab0-5ea9-a892-a02064d153af" :answer-field/key "$y=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :